// EXPECT: same signature and logic as
// IDCPY-ACCEPTS
// `a + 0` is `a`: an identity operation over an integer literal fingerprints
// as its surviving operand (compiler/parse/mid/form/unique/canon/expr/more/const),
// so this is the same duplicate the `a` vs `a + 1` case in duplicate_logic.id
// is, one op away. idc.py has no such rule and keeps the two functions
// distinct.
same(int a) { int r = a; } return int r;
plus_zero(int a) { int r = a + 0; } return int r;
